+/*
+**	OpenCNC3D: SHOTS FIRED SINCE THE LAST DUMP.
+**
+**	TechnoClass::Fire_At calls OpenCNC3D_Note_Fire once for every projectile it launches,
+**	visible or not, which is the one place a shot is certain: an anim is only spawned for
+**	the weapons that have one, and a small-arms round can be launched and spent inside a
+**	single tick without ever being seen in flight. Each record is the firer's heap id and
+**	kind (the same pair an EFX|ANIM line calls attref/attkind), the weapon (0 primary, 1
+**	secondary), the barrel of a two-shooter (the IsSecondShot the shot left with), the
+**	projectile's heap id, BulletType and name (two types share the name "DRAGON"), and
+**	the coordinate the engine launched it from.
